.SH NAME
anpu - ANPU — Guard what you build. Open-source web security intelligence.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
ANPU is an authorized web security analysis and attack-surface
intelligence tool. It orchestrates existing security tools (Nuclei,
OWASP ZAP) alongside its own passive analyzers, and
combines the results into a single, understandable security report.

.PP
ANPU must only be used against targets you own or are explicitly
authorized to test.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for anpu

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


